{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1565644401,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUyMDU5NzcxOQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3596#issuecomment-520597719"},"message":"That build uses the latest GitPython (v3.0.0), which has issues (gh-3598), so perhaps this is another one.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1565712837,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUyMDkwMjYwMg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3596#issuecomment-520902602"},"message":"uff, indeed smells like one more indeed","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1565725991,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUyMDk4MzUzMQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3596#issuecomment-520983531"},"message":"still failed to reproduce locally while using GitPython from git (so v3), grr :-/","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1565807006,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUyMTM2MTM2Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3596#issuecomment-521361362"},"message":"and really the error is a mystery since invocation seems to be correct, so not clear why `git` vomits with its \"usage:\" output upon running\n```\n/usr/lib/git-annex.linux/git fetch --progress --prune --recurse-submodules=no -v public\n```\nthe only possible reason is outdated (system?) git, but according to versions:\n```\ncmd:bundled-git=2.20.1 cmd:git=2.20.1 cmd:system-git=2.21.0\n```\nso the only difference is that system git is actually NEWER!  I do not have 2.21.0 readily available but installed `1:2.23.0~rc1-1` from debian - no problem running \n```\ngit fetch --progress --prune --recurse-submodules=no -v origin   \n```\nand also above it is full path  to bundled git... mystery mystery","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1565830763,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUyMTQ3NDU1OQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3596#issuecomment-521474559"},"message":"\u003e and really the error is a mystery since invocation seems to be correct, so not clear why `git` vomits with its \"usage:\" output upon running\n\nYeah, it's odd.  I found [a hint][0] about what's going on.\n\nSo I think the `git-{receive,update}-pack` call from remote (localhost here) is failing (with some message that starts with \"usage\" :).\n\nAnyway, I've tried to debug this on origin/scratch/receive-pack (tldr: I really didn't figure anything out but do have a bit more of an error message).  I switched to using `_git_custom_command` directly to remove gitpython from the equation.  I also followed up with the debugging command suggested in that stackoverflow question.\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\n\u003csummary\u003edetails\u003c/summary\u003e\n\nHere's the output I'm seeing in those runs:\n\n```\n# https://travis-ci.org/datalad/datalad/builds/572016409#L1242\nCommandError: command '['git', 'fetch', '--progress', '--prune', '--recurse-submodules=no', '-v', 'public']' failed with exitcode 128\nFailed to run ['git', 'fetch', '--progress', '--prune', '--recurse-submodules=no', '-v', 'public'] under '/tmp/datalad_demo_nipype.jZwf/datasets-tests.datalad.org'. Exit code=128. out= err=[ERROR] unknown arguments: ['-o', \"git-upload-pack '/tmp/datalad_demo_nipype_published.xRIA'\"] \n\nfatal: protocol error: bad line length character: usag\n\n[ERROR] unknown arguments: ['-o', \"git-upload-pack '/tmp/datalad_demo_nipype_published.xRIA'\"] \nfatal: protocol error: bad line length character: usag\n00926b154b78dfe892d7a1938cbe31acdf6b732a71b4 refs/heads/git-annexreport-status delete-refs side-band-64k quiet atomic ofs-delta agent=git/2.21.0\n0000\n```\n\nIt's hard to distinguish because I stupidly printed stdout/stderr again, but it looks like the direct `ssh localhost git-receive-pack \"$PUBLISHDIR\"` call isn't showing the error.  Swapping in `ssh localhost git-update-pack \"$PUBLISHDIR\"` also doesn't trigger the issue:\n\n```\n# https://travis-ci.org/datalad/datalad/builds/572016409#L1242\nCommandError: command '['git', 'fetch', '--progress', '--prune', '--recurse-submodules=no', '-v', 'public']' failed with exitcode 128\nFailed to run ['git', 'fetch', '--progress', '--prune', '--recurse-submodules=no', '-v', 'public'] under '/tmp/datalad_demo_nipype.jZwf/datasets-tests.datalad.org'. Exit code=128. out= err=[ERROR] unknown arguments: ['-o', \"git-upload-pack '/tmp/datalad_demo_nipype_published.xRIA'\"] \n\nfatal: protocol error: bad line length character: usag\n\n[ERROR] unknown arguments: ['-o', \"git-upload-pack '/tmp/datalad_demo_nipype_published.xRIA'\"] \nfatal: protocol error: bad line length character: usag\n00926b154b78dfe892d7a1938cbe31acdf6b732a71b4 refs/heads/git-annexreport-status delete-refs side-band-64k quiet atomic ofs-delta agent=git/2.21.0\n0000\n```\n\nSo I guess the new thing from above is `[ERROR] unknown arguments: ['-o', \"git-upload-pack '/tmp/datalad_demo_nipype_published.xRIA'\"]`.  I don't know where that's happening.\n\nTwo other things to note:\n\n  * The failure in the -neuroimaging repo seems to correspond with Travis's switch from Trusty to Xenial. \n  * It hasn't started yet, but I pushed a change to that branch to see what happens if we use the latest Git: https://travis-ci.org/datalad/datalad/builds/572091590\n\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\n[0]: https://stackoverflow.com/questions/8170436/git-remote-error-fatal-protocol-error-bad-line-length-character-unab","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1565971530,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUyMjA2MjU5NA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3596#issuecomment-522062594"},"message":"I took another look at this hoping I could trigger it with the a xenial docker image (rastasheep/ubuntu-sshd:16.04).  I installed git-annex-standalone and then Git 2.21.0 (from source) in that container.  That's of course not exactly the setup on Travis, but I figured that had a chance of catching a weird interaction between the remote and bundled git versions.\n\nI tried to\n\n  * fetch locally using the git bundled with git-annex (7.20190730+git2-ga63bf35dc-1~ndall+1)\n  * `ssh HOST git-{receive,upload}-pack REPO`.\n  * call `create-sibling`\n\nI didn't have any luck triggering an issue with any of those.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1565972197,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUyMjA2NjEyOQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3596#issuecomment-522066129"},"message":"I feel like we should eventually move away from magical travis environments to something more \"reproducible\".  Either running on travis but all steps in a container or just migrate to circle-ci altogether since docker image  to run tests in just a part of the spec, and it is possible (IIRC) get those original circle-ci images locally as well.  For this one probably we are doomed to backdoor travis again to get into that environment","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1565972410,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUyMjA2NzI3NA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3596#issuecomment-522067274"},"message":"Yes ^^^","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1566203254,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUyMjQ2NzI4NA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3596#issuecomment-522467284"},"message":"Found this last week:\n\nhttps://docs.travis-ci.com/user/running-build-in-debug-mode/","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1566223977,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUyMjU5MzU3OA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3596#issuecomment-522593578"},"message":"did you try it @bpoldrack ? it used to\n- be at least available only for .com (paid) travis subscriptions.\n- drop into terminal before actually running any commands so you had to manually invoke all those steps as described in https://docs.travis-ci.com/user/running-build-in-debug-mode/#things-to-do-once-you-are-inside-the-debug-vm\n- just crashed on me when I tried (it was probably a year or two ago)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1566441555,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUyMzcyMjg5MQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3596#issuecomment-523722891"},"message":"Since it started to infect other projects (reproman), we better differ it out. if we  get one test to reliably fail, we could try checking if downgrade of gitpython doesn't resolve it","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1566480530,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUyMzkwNjQzNA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3596#issuecomment-523906434"},"message":"\u003e if we  get one test to reliably fail, we could try checking if downgrade of gitpython doesn't resolve it\n\nIt's not a test, but as I mentioned above I've put the failing -neuroimaging example into the [scratch/receive-pack][0] branch.  All the other tests are removed.  In that branch, I switched the failing fetch call in update.py to use _git_custom_command(), but the failure still happens.  That indicates that it's probably not related to the newer gitpython.\n\nBut for completeness, today I updated that branch to downgrade the gitpython version.  The same failure happens:  https://travis-ci.org/datalad/datalad/builds/575331371\n\n[0]: https://github.com/datalad/datalad/compare/0.11.x...scratch/receive-pack","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1566481364,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUyMzkxMTk5Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3596#issuecomment-523911992"},"message":"Thanks! Sorry I have missed it.\nThen it must be git (installation) problem. We could at least check if it is a standard Ubuntu provided git they have, or may be they have some shim git script in addition","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1566481483,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUyMzkxMjc3NA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3596#issuecomment-523912774"},"message":"Hey - reproman trace the beast?!! ;-)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1566483609,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUyMzkyNzIyNg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3596#issuecomment-523927226"},"message":"Re travis debug: @yarikoptic, didn't try yet, no. It's just news to me that the feature is available at all. And the docs say one can request it for public repos as well.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1566486429,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUyMzk0NjUzMQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3596#issuecomment-523946531"},"message":"OK, some progress.  It's some interaction with `GIT_SSH_COMMAND='datalad sshrun'`.\n\n---\n\nAs mentioned above, the \"usag\" bit is some output being taken as part of the protocol.  In the error message, we can see\n\n```\n[ERROR] unknown arguments: ['-o', \"git-upload-pack '/tmp/datalad_demo_nipype_published.xRIA'\"]\n```\n\nStarting with \"[ERROR] \", that is very likely coming from datalad and almost certainly not coming from git or git-annex.  The only place we call log.error() with  \"unknown arguments: \" is cmdline/main.py:\n\nhttps://github.com/datalad/datalad/blob/9846080f7c011ae024bef5f274096c87bf097e64/datalad/cmdline/main.py#L463-L469\n\nTo verify that that is the stop, I printed something to stdout before `cmdlineargs.subparser.print_usage()`, and the first four printed characters showed up in the protocol error instead of \"usag\": https://travis-ci.org/datalad/datalad/builds/575364833#L1220\n\nAnd the mostly likely datalad command to be running with a fetch/push is \"datalad sshrun\".  Setting `GIT_SSH_COMMAND` to \"ssh\"\n\nhttps://github.com/datalad/datalad/blob/a2bbe84b8b1da6920f20550afa3f1cc935ca98e5/datalad/consts.py#L65\n\nremoved the failure: https://travis-ci.org/datalad/datalad/builds/575373273\n\nThat of course doesn't explain what is actually triggering the failure, what about the Travis switch to Xenial is making it show up, or why it isn't showing up in the other spots where `datalad sshrun` is used with localhost (e.g., the create-sibling tests).","files":null},{"type":6,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1566486429,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDI2NzQyMzM2Mw=="},"target":"b874c71cef179f355da9c9e66fa99226acc6f3471c1a513732b13cd5f8cd80cb","message":"OK, some progress.  It's some interaction with `GIT_SSH_COMMAND='datalad sshrun'`.\n\n---\n\nAs mentioned above, the \"usag\" bit is some output being taken as part of the protocol.  In the error message, we can see\n\n```\n[ERROR] unknown arguments: ['-o', \"git-upload-pack '/tmp/datalad_demo_nipype_published.xRIA'\"]\n```\n\nStarting with \"[ERROR] \", that is very likely coming from datalad and almost certainly not coming from git or git-annex.  The only place we call log.error() with  \"unknown arguments: \" is cmdline/main.py:\n\nhttps://github.com/datalad/datalad/blob/9846080f7c011ae024bef5f274096c87bf097e64/datalad/cmdline/main.py#L463-L469\n\nTo verify that that is the spot, I printed something to stdout before `cmdlineargs.subparser.print_usage()`, and the first four printed characters showed up in the protocol error instead of \"usag\": https://travis-ci.org/datalad/datalad/builds/575364833#L1220\n\nAnd the mostly likely datalad command to be running with a fetch/push is \"datalad sshrun\".  Setting `GIT_SSH_COMMAND` to \"ssh\"\n\nhttps://github.com/datalad/datalad/blob/a2bbe84b8b1da6920f20550afa3f1cc935ca98e5/datalad/consts.py#L65\n\nremoved the failure: https://travis-ci.org/datalad/datalad/builds/575373273\n\nThat of course doesn't explain what is actually triggering the failure, what about the Travis switch to Xenial is making it show up, or why it isn't showing up in the other spots where `datalad sshrun` is used with localhost (e.g., the create-sibling tests).","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1566489974,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUyMzk3MDYzNA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3596#issuecomment-523970634"},"message":"\u003e That of course doesn't explain what is actually triggering the failure,\n\nThe ssh call that is failing is\n\n```\n# https://travis-ci.org/datalad/datalad/builds/575409570#L1226\n['/home/travis/virtualenv/python3.5.6/bin/datalad', 'sshrun', '-o', 'SendEnv=GIT_PROTOCOL', 'localhost', \"git-upload-pack '/tmp/datalad_demo_nipype_published.3E6l'\"]\n```\n\nWe need to update sshrun to understand `-o` if we want to substitute it for `GIT_SSH_COMMAND`.\n\n\u003e what about the Travis switch to Xenial is making it show up,\n\nTrusty had Git 2.15.1.  The use of `-o` seems to have been added in Git v2.16.0, specifically 0c2f0d2703 (connect: tell server that the client understands v1, 2017-10-16).\n\n\u003e or why it isn't showing up in the other spots where `datalad sshrun` is used with localhost (e.g., the create-sibling tests)\n\nDunno.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1566492406,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUyMzk4NTUwOA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3596#issuecomment-523985508"},"message":"\u003e We need to update sshrun to understand `-o` if we want to substitute it for `GIT_SSH_COMMAND`.\n\nConfirmed with c80b9c16a that this resolved the issue: https://travis-ci.org/datalad/datalad/builds/575428381\n\nLater today I'll clean up those sshrun changes and submit a PR.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1566497828,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUyNDAxOTAyMQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3596#issuecomment-524019021"},"message":"Well done detective @kyleam!!!","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1566584097,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MjU4MDQ3MjA3Nw=="},"status":2}]}